************ Azure AD B2B service ****************
* Azure AD B2B is used to share application and services with guest users.
* Any external user/ organization trying to access Azure AD, may or may not have Azure AD account and still they can access.
* B2B uses an email invitation & redemption process (like NIMs) in order to authenticate any external user.
* By using B2B service, we don't need to manage external account or password details.
* Any guest user can be added to Azure AD via Azure AD portal (provided user had Admin permission)
* App owner (for NIMs) or group owner (for external user group) can be asigned to manage guest user accounts.
* If external user is only interested in free Azure AD features, then licensing is not required. but if wants to access licensing
  features, then we can add 5 users / license. 

