********* Azure AD domain services (ADDS) ************
Azure AD domain services are managed version of traditional on-prem Azure AD. It offers domain join, group policy, LDAP, 
NTLM authentication. It does   not require any deployemnet of domain controls. 
* It works with existing Azure AD tenant. Example-
		- compatable with cloud only Azure AD tenants.
		- compatable with Azure AD tenants that are in sync with on-prem AD.
		- Users synced into Azure AD from on-prem , can be found in Azure AD services.
*When ADDS is deployed, a managed domain is created on virtual network that adds to windows server domain controllers in VM.
 Not one can access those windows server domain controllers. Only Azure manages it on its own. 
 
* When we add resources to Azure AD, ADDS can sync those details but if we add resources in ADDS , Azure AD will not have those 
details. So it's always adviced to add resources to Azure AD and let it sync to ADDS on it's own.
* ADDS is tightly integrated with Azure AD. Hence ADDS can sync AD users automatically.
* External accounts that are linked to Azure AD , will not be available in ADDS. 
* It allows us to deploy applications that rely on windows integrated authentication.
* Since ADDS includes multiple domain controllers, the managed domain is always available. Never goes for downtime.
* ADDS can work in standard alone.

